Strategy: // CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// Spider text-to-SQL usually has a long unconstrained preamble (schema/question
// text and possibly explanatory tokens) followed by one SQL query region that
// should obey the schema-specialized SQL grammar. This strategy therefore
// tracks only the standard delimiter state: whether generation is currently
// inside the constrained SQL span, and the current constrained SQL prefix.
// Outside the span it generates in chunks until either EOS or the opening
// delimiter "<<" appears. Inside the span it uses two constrained modes chosen
// from parser observations: when the valid-next set is narrow, it uses an
// adaptive/group-boosted single-token step to softly favor caller-supplied
// token groups; when the valid-next set is wide, it uses ConstrainedSymbol to
// let the model emit a larger grammar-valid symbol with less per-token
// interference. Once the parser reports a complete SQL prefix, it closes the
// span immediately.
//
// The tracked constrained prefix is exactly the suffix of generated that lies
// between delimiters, so every constrained helper can be called with a parser-
// valid prefix and the verifier can re-establish that the generated output
// still ends with the active SQL fragment. This matches the task: one SQL
// query, grammar-checked against the current schema, with EOS terminating
// generation at any point.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity:
// - Outside-span chunk branch: if no open-span token is seen, insideConstrainedOut
//   stays false so the implication is vacuous; if stoppedOnOpenSpan is true we
//   set currentConstrainedOut := [], which is valid by the method precondition
//   parser.IsValidPrefix([]).
// - Complete-prefix branch: CloseConstrainedSpan returns insideOut == false and
//   currentOut == [], so the implication becomes vacuous.
// - Narrow constrained branch: AdaptiveConstrainedStep returns either eosToken
//   or a token whose append keeps parser validity; on non-EOS,
//   AppendConstrainedToken yields parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut).
// - Wide constrained branch: ConstrainedSymbol directly ensures the returned
//   currentOut is a parser-valid prefix; assigning currentConstrainedOut to it
//   preserves the invariant.
//
// suffix:
// - Outside-span chunk branch: when insideConstrainedOut remains false the
//   implication is vacuous; when an open span is entered we set
//   currentConstrainedOut := [], and the length-0 suffix of generated is [].
// - Complete-prefix branch: CloseConstrainedSpan appends the closing delimiter
//   and resets currentConstrainedOut to [], so the implication is vacuous.
// - Narrow constrained branch: AppendConstrainedToken appends the same non-EOS
//   token to both generated and currentConstrainedOut, preserving that the
//   latter is the suffix of the former.
// - Wide constrained branch: with stablePrefix := generated[..|generated| -
//   |currentConstrainedOut|], we assign generated := stablePrefix + symbolOut
//   and currentConstrainedOut := symbolOut, so generated's last |symbolOut|
//   tokens are exactly currentConstrainedOut.
//
// progress:
// - Outside-span chunk branch appends at most stepsUsed tokens and we do
//   steps := steps + stepsUsed; therefore |generated| grows by at most the same
//   amount, preserving |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps.
// - Complete-prefix branch appends at most one token and increments steps by 1.
// - Narrow constrained branch either breaks on EOS or appends exactly one token
//   via AppendConstrainedToken and increments steps by 1.
// - Wide constrained branch uses ConstrainedSymbol, then increments steps by
//   stepsUsed; generated is rebuilt from stablePrefix plus symbolOut, whose
//   growth over the old constrained suffix is bounded by the helper's consumed
//   steps, so the linear bound is preserved. Every non-breaking branch strictly
//   increases steps, satisfying decreases maxSteps - steps.
//
// cost accounting:
// - The loop keeps cost == 0 as an invariant and uses a separate local steps
//   counter for the returned accounting.
// - UnconstrainedChunk and ConstrainedSymbol internally bump helper cost by
//   stepsUsed, while CloseConstrainedSpan and AdaptiveConstrainedStep each bump
//   by 1; we mirror that with steps := steps + stepsUsed or steps := steps + 1.
// - AppendConstrainedToken is non-bumping, so in the narrow branch the only
//   charged action is AdaptiveConstrainedStep and steps still increases by 1.
// - Break branches do not need further preservation because the loop exits;
//   after the loop we return cost := steps, hence cost <= maxSteps.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END
generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
cost := 0;

var steps: nat := 0;
var narrowThreshold: nat := 12;

while steps < maxSteps
  invariant 0 <= steps <= maxSteps
  invariant lm.ValidTokensIdsLogits()
  invariant !insideConstrainedOut ==> currentConstrainedOut == []
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> |currentConstrainedOut| <= |generated|
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> generated[|generated| - |currentConstrainedOut|..] == currentConstrainedOut
  invariant |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
