// tracks only the standard delimiter state: whether generation is currently
// inside the constrained SQL span, and the current constrained SQL prefix.
// Outside the span it generates in chunks until either EOS or the opening
// delimiter "<<" appears. Inside the span it uses two constrained modes chosen
// from parser observations: when the valid-next set is narrow, it uses an
// adaptive/group-boosted single-token step to softly favor caller-supplied
// token groups; when the valid-next set is wide, it uses ConstrainedSymbol to
// let the model emit a larger grammar-valid symbol with less per-token
// interference. Once the parser reports a complete SQL prefix, it closes the
// span immediately.
//
